The RRO 3.2.2 rpm for RHEL6 should be relocatable.

CRAN is a collection of sites, carrying the same content (R distributions, extensions, documentation, packages, binaries).

MRAN is Microsoft's site where you can find information about R, download Revolution R Open, and look up R Packages. MRAN includes tools to explore R Packages <http://mran.revolutionanalytics.com/packages/> and R Task Views <http://mran.revolutionanalytics.com/taskview/>, making it easy to find packages to extend R's capabilities. It also provides access to daily snapshots of the packages on CRAN to increase the reproducibility of your scripts. MRAN is updated daily.

RRO is an enhanced distribution of R. Enhancements include multi-core processing <https://mran.revolutionanalytics.com/rro/#intelmkl1>, a fixed CRAN repository <https://mran.revolutionanalytics.com/rro/#repos> date, and reproducible R <https://mran.revolutionanalytics.com/rro/#checkpoint> with the checkpoint package. RRO 3.2.2 includes R 3.2.2,  and is therefore fully compatibility with all packages, scripts and applications that work with that version of R.

Cheers,
Josee Martens

