From: u9ca0345d553844f2 at groups.google.com (=?utf-8?q?Jos=C3=A9e_Martens?=)
Date: Wed, 20 Jan 2016 00:51:57 +0000
Subject: Microsoft R Open (MRO) 3.2.3 now available
Message-ID: <o_LD5pmS_UQ.DTf52VS7CQAJ@rropen.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rropen/c/o_LD5pmS_UQ/m/DTf52VS7CQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Microsoft R Open <https://mran.microsoft.com/rro/> 3.2.3, the enhanced open source R distribution from Microsoft, is now available for download. <https://mran.microsoft.com/download/> Revolution R Open is now known as Microsoft R Open (MRO).

This update brings multi-threaded performance <https://mran.microsoft.com/documents/rro/multithread/> to the latest update to the R engine from the R Core Group <https://www.r-project.org/contributors.html>, which includes several improvements and bug fixes <https://mran.microsoft.com/news/#r323>. Significant amongst these is default support for HTTPS connections, making it easy to follow the best practices for R security <http://blog.revolutionanalytics.com/2015/08/good-advice-for-security-with-r.html> recommended by the R Consortium. The checkpoint package <https://mran.microsoft.com/documents/rro/reproducibility/#timemachine> included with Microsoft R Open likewise uses HTTPS when downloading R package versions for reproducible data analysis.

MRO 3.2.3 is available for download now for Windows, Mac and Linux systems <https://mran.microsoft.com/documents/rro/installation/#sysreq>, and is 100% compatible <https://mran.microsoft.com/rro/#compatible> with R 3.2.3.

You can download Microsoft R Open now from the link below, and we welcome comments, suggestions and other discussion on this forum.  If you're new to Microsoft R Open, here are some tips to get started, <https://mran.microsoft.com/documents/getting-started/> and there are many data sources you can explore with MRO <https://mran.microsoft.com/documents/data/>. Thanks go as always to the contributors to the R Project <https://mran.revolutionanalytics.com/documents/what-is-r/#contributors> upon which RRO is built.

MRAN: Download Microsoft R Open <https://mran.revolutionanalytics.com/download/>

Regards,

— Josée

