Hi Giovanni,

I am not sure why this error occurs for some users on Windows, but we are investigating the problem.
For now you can work around the issue by downloading and installing the 64-bit Visual C++ Redistributable.

See this information:
http://www.faqforge.com/windows/fix-the-program-cant-start-because-msvcr100-dll-is-missing-from-your-computer-error-on-windows/

Just make sure that the file 'msvcr120.dll' is installed in both the Windows 'system32' and 'SYSWOW64' directories under 'C:\Windows', then try
rerunning the Windows MKL installer and things should work.

Stephen Weller
Microsoft R Open Technical Support

